=====================
Form factor asymmetry
=====================

. Only a finite part of the crystal ED is used to make
  the aspherical atomic form factors. So it may occur
  that the FFs are not symmetric under the space group.
  Therefore symmetrization is performed.

. The root-mean squared asymmetry in the form factors
  per reflection) is reported, for each asymm. unit atom.

   (RMS asymmetry)^2 = (1/n_refl) Sum_k |F_k-sym(F_k)|^2
    Max asymmetry    = Max_k |F_k-sym(F_k)|, at (h,k,l)

  It should be zero, to at least 5 d.p's.
